# Godot scenes and serialized resources

- **Do not** edit `*.tscn` files (or other Godot serialized scene text) in the repo.
- **Do not** edit `*.tres` / other Godot serialized **resource** text on disk (same policy as scenes), including adding new `.tres` files via the agent.
- If the UI, scene tree, or resource data needs changes, **describe the steps** for the user to apply in the **Godot Editor** (which nodes to add, which properties to set, export paths, which `.tres` to create or adjust, etc.).
- It is fine to edit **C# scripts** (`.cs`) that attach to scenes or define `[GlobalClass]` resources; avoid changing serialized scene/resource data on disk when the user prefers editor-owned content.
